# p2_scores.py (deterministic)

== A. truth x = 0; forecasts uniform on 5 points
   forecast                                   LS     CRPS CRPS(int)    CRIGN   ES_0.5
   near {-2,...,2}                        2.3219   0.4000   0.4000   2.1178   0.4174
   scattered {-20,-10,0,10,20}            2.3219   4.0000   4.0000  21.1779   1.3200
   scattered {-37,0,12,55,81}             2.3219  13.7200  13.7200  67.8341   2.2574
   scattered, 0.21 on the truth           2.2515   3.9006   3.9006  20.8484   1.2872
   -> LS equal (log2 5) for the three uniform forecasts; CRPS, CRIGN, ES grow with the spread.
   -> B. 'scattered, 0.21 on the truth' has the lower LS (2.2515 < 2.3219) and the higher CRPS: opposite rankings.

== C. truth P = 0.5 N(-1, 0.1^2) + 0.5 N(1, 0.1^2); family N(0, s^2) (misspecified)
   log-optimal scale: closed form sqrt(E X^2) = 1.004988, numerical 1.004988
   CRPS-optimal scale: 1.202984
   N(0, s_log^2)    expected LS = 2.05427 bits (density), expected CRPS = 0.60447
   N(0, s_crps^2)   expected LS = 2.09580 bits (density), expected CRPS = 0.59725
   -> LS prefers N(0, s_log^2), CRPS prefers N(0, s_crps^2): both proper, opposite rankings of two wrong forecasts.
